      "delivery": "Rook exposes a personal liability with reluctant precision; give each admission weight without asking for sympathy.",
      "returnToBaseAfter": true,
      "from": "\"Yes,\" said Rook. \"I'm building something in the four of you on purpose. I started doing it about ten days ago, in a field, on a morning after a fire, and I did not decide to do it in advance, and I have not stopped since. You're right that it has stages. You're right that it's a course. You're right that I never asked, and you're right that it wasn't mine to not ask, and I'm not going to argue with a single word of it, because I've been standing in front of you for a fortnight knowing exactly what I was doing and telling myself that four children who can hold a line don't need the reason.",
      "through": "\"And yes. There's a reason. There's one reason and it's the whole of it and it isn't a general one about the road or the winter or the state of the world. It's mine. It's the most personal thing there is about me.\"",
      "paragraphs": [
        31,
        32
      ],
      "reason": "Rook confirms that the course is intentional and rooted in his most private motive."
    },
