      "from": "\"That's a good offer,\" she said. \"It's a very good offer, and it's the second time you've made it, and I'd like everybody here to notice that both times you've made it, it was about four minutes after somebody asked you something you didn't want to answer.\"",
      "through": "\"At the weigh-yard, you offered to hand us to a woman with a book,\" said Dessa. \"Today you're offering to hand us to a gate. And both times it's dressed up as you being decent, and both times what it actually is, is you arranging things so that the people who've got questions about you will be somebody else's problem before the questions come due.\"",
