      "returnToBaseAfter": true,
      "from": "\"Twenty-two nights ago, this man took the first watch. Then he took the second. Then he took most of the third, and he has done that every night since, and I have watched him do it from about four feet away, because I am an old woman who does not sleep, and there is nothing else to look at.\"",
      "through": "\"He is not resting. I don't mean he's tired; we're all tired. I mean that whatever he is doing up there on the bank, it costs him something to do, and he is spending it on four children and a cart every night for nothing, and he has not once mentioned it or asked for a thing in return or made any of you feel it.\" She looked at Wyck. \"You asked what you're standing in a line for. I don't know. But you've had twenty-two nights of a man paying for something, and I've been on this road long enough to tell you that when a person pays like that and won't say why, it is almost never because the reason does him credit.\"",
      "paragraphs": [
